<title>BELGIUM: SIBEKA H1 1996 GROUP NET PROFIT FALLS.</title>
<headline>SIBEKA H1 1996 GROUP NET PROFIT FALLS.</headline>
<text>
<p>BRUSSELS, Sept 18, Reuter - Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excluding minorities)	 136 vs   268</p>
<p>    Cons net					 150 vs   285</p>
<p>    Cash flow					328 vs   455</p>
<p>    Turnover				     4,959 vs 4,821</p>
<p>    Operating profit				90 vs   255</p>
<p>    Taxes					     18 vs    16</p>
<p>    Current profit				 167 vs   312</p>
<p>    Non-cons net				   201 vs   147</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian diamond tools group Sibeka, a unit of Belgian</p>
<p>non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere SA (UM), said</p>
<p>the fall in profit reflected the economic deterioration which</p>
<p>depressed profits of its Diamant Boart diamond tool unit, and to</p>
<p>a lesser extent the lower profit of the Megapode group.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
